# The image is published to a public registry (GHCR), so this is an allowlist:
# everything is out unless named below. backend/ holds production secrets
# (.env), real data in the local fallback files (data/*.json, data/backups/),
# and downloaded or generated artefacts (f1db, f1_cache, reports, .venv). A
# denylist would ship the next such file the day someone adds it.
#
# What goes in is the git-tracked code the API and its one-shot jobs run:
#   main.py, app/       the API
#   scripts/            jobs run with the same image (power-unit ingest, backfills)
#   data/raw/           the FIA regulation PDFs: the rulebook ingest reads them,
#                       and the API checks which seasons' rules exist
#   models/…joblib      the trained race predictor the API serves
#   requirements*.txt   what the image installs
# Tests, tooling, the MCP server and dev configs stay out: nothing in the
# container runs them.
*
!main.py
!app/
!scripts/
!data/raw/
!models/race_predictor.joblib
!requirements.txt
!requirements-ingest.txt

# Never, even inside an allowed directory.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.DS_Store
**/.env
**/.env.*
